 (dest/'design-precedent.md').write_text(f'''# Recovered design precedent\n\nStarting source: `{source}`. Owner export in docs/theme-verification/approved-decisions.md approves DM-001 through DM-010 and explicitly selects B, Botanical Charcoal. Commit bc64621 implements that decision. The original dark audit targets 952ab1b; proposals A/C were alternatives, not separately recorded owner rejections. No decision export is missing.\n\nInherited decisions: paired semantic roles, distinct action foreground/background, restrained surfaces, clear focus, serif/body/identifier typography, care/tag identities and light/public/print boundaries. We retained those foundations and every pre-existing dark token, and added theme-aware chart/graph roles without introducing a new provider or client calculations.\n\nIndependent light-mode judgment: warm solid canvas/cards rather than layered cream transparency, quieter card shadows, stronger meaningful control boundaries, readable metadata, a light chart surface and no whole-card text opacity. The brief's illustrative colors were evaluated; its light direction informs these choices but is not misrepresented as an earlier owner decision.\n\nIntentional dark delta: chart warning/resolved symbol foreground changes for contrast. Data, layout, business rules and typography are unchanged.\n''')
 (dest/'executive-summary.md').write_text(f'''# Light-mode refinement\n\nSource `{source}`. Implemented eight consolidated findings using the approved Botanical Charcoal design precedent and a complementary warm botanical light foundation. No live deployment or schema/business-logic changes.\n\nVerified scope: {len(routes)} route templates with desktop/mobile before/after light captures; {len(da['routes'])} representative dark route templates; {len(sb)} baseline and {len(sa)} after conditional/component captures across both themes. Routes have explicit status; three redirects are not interior reviews. {len(inventory['components'])} component files source-inventoried.\n\nShared fields: boundary 1.71→3.67:1. Small care/exhibit metadata failures are corrected by shared secondary/muted roles. Normal marketing action text: 3.34→4.92:1. Care/tag palettes remain unchanged. Metric charts now integrate with light surfaces, with corrected symbol pairs.\n\nScreenshots are fictional local fixtures. The full portable gallery stays outside Git to avoid large deployment downloads. Limitations and validation details are in validation-report.md.\n''')
